// Regression: a member call `x.load(y)` on a receiver without that method
// silently resolved to a same-named GLOBAL (host function `load`) with the
// receiver prepended, so `image.load(path)` on a plain bool (the return of
// extension.load) dispatched to the module loader's host `load` with 2 args
// and threw "Host function 'load' expects 1 arguments, got 2".
// The script-global CALL_METHOD fallback must apply to pipe stages only
// (`data |> doubled` = doubled(data)); inherited-member-call syntax keeps its
// null result. Expected: bool method call returns null; a pipe still passes
// the piped value as the global fn's first argument. Exit 0.
image = true
img = image.load("/home/all/Pictures/photo.jpg")
assert(img == null, "method call on bool without the method must return null, not hit the global")

fn doubled(x) { x + x }
a = "ab"
r1 = a |> doubled
assert(r1 == "abab", "pipe stage still calls the script global with the piped value first")
r2 = "hello" |> len()
assert(r2 == 5, "pipe stage still reaches prototype methods")

return 0